"""Susan Grimshaw, part A: biography (Origins, Red Dead Redemption 2 chapters 1 to 6, epilogue grave).

Sources (Red Dead Wiki EN, Oct 2026, saved in scratchpad cov/susan/ and cov/susan/m/): character page "Susan
Grimshaw" (History, Mission Appearances, Murders Committed, Trivia); FR page "Susan Grimshaw" (fr.txt); mission
transcripts "Outlaws from the West/dialogues" (cabin orders, room assignments at the end of the mission), "Eastward
Bound/dialogues" (Mary-Beth's book, Arthur's tent, Tilly), "Polite Society, Valentine Style/dialogues" (Mary-Beth and
Karen about Grimshaw), "Exit, Pursued by a Bruised Ego/dialogues" (EPBE_dlg.txt: "Susan sent them out scouting"), "Who
is Not Without Sin/dialogues" (Swanson brought back), "Blessed are the Peacemakers/dialogues" (Arthur put to bed),
"The Battle of Shady Belle/dialogues" (Milton at Clemens Point, arrival at Shady Belle), "Red Dead Redemption
(mission)/dialogues" (packing, standoff, death; Arthur's "Not Molly... not Miss Grimshaw... not even Colm.").
Mission pages (no transcript on the wiki): "No, No and Thrice, No" (story, gold medal tips, deaths, notes, trivia on
the ride dialogue), "Horsemen, Apocalypses" (non-fighters go inside; gallery caption naming Susan in the house),
"That's Murfree Country" (Molly's death, chapter 5), "We Loved Once and True I" (fetched: Susan tells Arthur about
Mary's letter), "Eastward Bound" (trivia: Grimshaw sends Lenny and Micah scouting), "Fleeting Joy", "Enter, Pursued
by a Memory", "A Strange Kindness", "Blood Feuds, Ancient and Modern" (none names her); "Paying Respects" (fetched:
grave location and availability after "Simple Pleasures"); "Camp Events" (Lakay packing order). Real world:
Wikipedia "List of Red Dead Redemption 2 characters" (wp_list.txt), citing the official guide (Price 2018, p. 372) for
her length of membership and USgamer for Charles burying her.
Cross-checked against the fact-checked parts arthur_A/C, charles_A, dutch_A/C, micah_A, javier_A, john_A, abigail_A,
jack_A, lenny_A, sadie_A, uncle_A, bill_A: Milton's three days are conditional on Dutch surrendering (uncle rule);
That's Murfree Country closes chapter 5; Molly shot with a shotgun (arthur_C says pump-action: the type is left out
here, the mission page only says "shotgun"); Milton tells Arthur the Pinkertons "sweated" Molly and she said nothing
(arthur_C); Susan turns at Javier's warning and Micah shoots her (micah_A, javier_A, john_A); Charles buries Susan in
Roanoke Ridge (charles_A, arthur_C).
Contradiction noted: arthur_A says Susan "arrived after" Arthur; Wikipedia, summarizing the official guide, says she
has been in the gang "for as long as Arthur"; the Red Dead Wiki counts her among the original members with Dutch,
Hosea and Arthur. The text gives the two sources' versions, attributed, without settling it.
Contradiction noted: the character page says Susan urges Arthur to slit Anthony Foreman's throat; the mission page
says she tells him the choice is his. Both are given, attributed.

Ownership: official descriptions (Rockstar tweet of 6 Sep 2018, official guide wording), names ("Miss Grimshaw"),
appearance, weapons, personality, the relationship with Dutch and Annabelle, and camp scenes (Colter speech, John
in the cabin, dance with Dutch, Molly's mood, Sean's homecoming, the songs, Uncle's date, Micah's taunts, Mary-Beth
slapped, Karen calling her a murderer, Strauss's expulsion, the quarrel with Dutch at Beaver Hollow, Jack and Cain)
are part B; this part keeps a pointer clause at most. Mission lines quoted in part C (Quotes) are paraphrased here
without quotation marks. Kills are told here as events and listed in the C table.

Excluded: the fiancé, "best man she ever knew" (character page only, no source found in any transcript, camp event
or guide text; the wording matches Sadie's lines about her husband); "retired painted lady" in the credits (no copy
of the credits confirms it; left out of A, flagged for D); Susan sitting on Dutch's lap at poker (relationship, B,
and unsourced); "Dutch completely ignoring her death because he saw her siding with Arthur as treachery or was too
far gone" (interpretation; only the observable fact is kept: the transcript gives Dutch no word for her); "Susan's
actions caused a rift" and "most of the gang believing Molly got what she deserved" (generalization; reactions are
B's); Micah's slur in the room-assignment scene (paraphrased).
"""


def two(en, fr): return {"en": en, "fr": fr}


BLOCKS = [
    # ================================================================ Origins
    {"h3": two("Origins", "Origines"), "year": ""},
    {"p": two("The games give no birth date and no birthplace for Susan Grimshaw, and her life before the gang is not told in the story. The Red Dead Wiki counts her among the first members of the Van der Linde gang, with [[dutch-van-der-linde|Dutch van der Linde]], [[hosea-matthews|Hosea Matthews]] and [[arthur-morgan|Arthur Morgan]]; the official guide's account of her early years is quoted under Personality. For a time she was Dutch's partner (their relationship is covered under Relationships). By 1899 she runs the daily life of the camp.",
              "Les jeux ne donnent ni date ni lieu de naissance pour Susan Grimshaw, et l'histoire ne dit rien de sa vie avant le gang. Le Red Dead Wiki la range parmi les premiers membres du gang Van der Linde, avec [[dutch-van-der-linde|Dutch van der Linde]], [[hosea-matthews|Hosea Matthews]] et [[arthur-morgan|Arthur Morgan]] ; ce qu'en dit le guide officiel est cité dans la rubrique Personnalité. Elle a été un temps la compagne de Dutch (leur relation est traitée dans la rubrique Relations). En 1899, c'est elle qui fait tourner le camp au quotidien.")},

    # ================================================================ RDR2 1899
    {"h3": two("Red Dead Redemption 2 (1899)", "Red Dead Redemption 2 (1899)"), "year": "1899"},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 1: Colter", "Chapitre 1 : Colter"), "chapter": 1},
    {"p": two("After the failed ferry robbery in Blackwater, the gang flees into the snow of the mountains and takes shelter in Colter, an abandoned mining town. In \"Outlaws from the West\", as soon as Davey Callander's body is carried into the cabin, Susan hands out jobs: [[mary-beth-gaskill|Mary-Beth Gaskill]] is to light the fire, [[karen-jones|Karen Jones]] to bring every blanket the gang has, and the cook [[simon-pearson|Simon Pearson]] to see what food is left. Dutch then tells the group that they may stay a few days and asks Pearson and Miss Grimshaw to turn the place into a camp. At the end of the mission, Susan gives out the sleeping quarters. She sends Dutch to a cabin where [[molly-oshea|Molly O'Shea]] will show him the way and gives Arthur a room of his own. She puts [[micah-bell|Micah Bell]] in the building shared by the other men. Micah protests that Arthur gets a room while he gets a bunk next to [[bill-williamson|Bill Williamson]], and Hosea sends him to bed.",
              "Après l'échec du braquage du ferry à Blackwater, le gang fuit dans la neige des montagnes et se réfugie à Colter, une ville minière abandonnée. Dans \"Outlaws from the West\", dès que le corps de Davey Callander est porté dans la cabane, Susan distribue les tâches : [[mary-beth-gaskill|Mary-Beth Gaskill]] doit allumer le feu, [[karen-jones|Karen Jones]] rapporter toutes les couvertures disponibles, et le cuisinier [[simon-pearson|Simon Pearson]] faire l'inventaire de la nourriture. Dutch annonce ensuite qu'ils resteront peut-être quelques jours et charge Pearson et Miss Grimshaw de transformer l'endroit en camp. À la fin de la mission, Susan répartit les couchages. Elle envoie Dutch vers une cabane où [[molly-oshea|Molly O'Shea]] le conduira et attribue à Arthur une chambre pour lui seul. Elle installe [[micah-bell|Micah Bell]] dans le bâtiment des autres hommes. Micah s'indigne qu'Arthur ait droit à une chambre quand lui hérite d'une couchette à côté de [[bill-williamson|Bill Williamson]], et Hosea l'envoie se coucher.")},
    {"p": two("The Red Dead Wiki lists Susan in \"Enter, Pursued by a Memory\", but the transcript of that mission gives her no line. In \"Eastward Bound\", the gang loads its wagons in Colter, and Susan scolds Mary-Beth for reading instead of helping. When the gang reaches its new camp at Horseshoe Overlook, above Valentine, she walks Arthur to the tent the girls have set up for him. She tells him that most of his belongings from Blackwater were saved. Arthur points out that his money was not. When he adds that they can always make more, she answers that they are going to have to. On her way back she berates [[tilly-jackson|Tilly Jackson]] in coarse terms for doing a job badly.",
              "Le Red Dead Wiki fait figurer Susan dans \"Enter, Pursued by a Memory\", mais la transcription de cette mission ne lui prête aucune réplique. Dans \"Eastward Bound\", le gang charge ses chariots à Colter, et Susan reproche à Mary-Beth de lire au lieu de donner un coup de main. À l'arrivée au nouveau camp de Horseshoe Overlook, au-dessus de Valentine, elle conduit Arthur jusqu'à la tente que les filles lui ont préparée. Elle lui apprend que la plupart de ses affaires de Blackwater ont été sauvées. Arthur fait remarquer que son argent, lui, ne l'a pas été. Quand il ajoute qu'on peut toujours en gagner d'autre, elle répond qu'il va bien falloir. En repartant, elle s'en prend en termes crus à [[tilly-jackson|Tilly Jackson]], qui a mal fait son travail.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 2: Horseshoe Overlook", "Chapitre 2 : Horseshoe Overlook"), "chapter": 2},
    {"p": two("In \"Exit, Pursued by a Bruised Ego\", Arthur tells Hosea that Susan sent [[lenny-summers|Lenny Summers]] and Micah out scouting and that he expected them back by now. In \"Polite Society, Valentine Style\", Mary-Beth tells Arthur that the girls have been stuck in camp for two weeks and that Karen is close to murdering Grimshaw. Arthur asks whether Miss Grimshaw can spare them, Karen mocks him for worrying about chores, and he takes the women and [[uncle|Uncle]] to Valentine. In \"We Loved Once and True I\", Susan tells Arthur that a letter has come for him from [[mary-linton|Mary Linton]], in Valentine. According to the mission page, one of the girls collected it after Mary recognized her as a member of the gang.",
              "Dans \"Exit, Pursued by a Bruised Ego\", Arthur explique à Hosea que Susan a envoyé [[lenny-summers|Lenny Summers]] et Micah en reconnaissance et qu'il les attendait déjà de retour. Dans \"Polite Society, Valentine Style\", Mary-Beth confie à Arthur que les filles sont coincées au camp depuis deux semaines et que Karen n'est pas loin d'assassiner Grimshaw. Arthur demande si Miss Grimshaw peut se passer d'elles, Karen se moque de ce souci de corvées, et il emmène les femmes et [[uncle|Uncle]] à Valentine. Dans \"We Loved Once and True I\", Susan annonce à Arthur qu'une lettre de [[mary-linton|Mary Linton]] est arrivée pour lui, de Valentine. D'après la page de la mission, l'une des filles l'a récupérée après que Mary l'a reconnue comme membre du gang.")},
    {"p": two("At the end of \"Who is Not Without Sin\", Arthur brings [[orville-swanson|Reverend Swanson]] back from Flatneck Station, drunk, and drops him onto his bed. Susan comes over and asks what happened. Arthur answers that it was the usual. She pities Swanson, thanks Arthur and says she will keep an eye on him. The Red Dead Wiki also lists her in \"A Strange Kindness\", the mission that leads to the gang's move south to Clemens Point, but the mission page does not name her. The camp scenes of this chapter, among them [[sean-macguire|Sean MacGuire]]'s homecoming party, are covered under Relationships.",
              "À la fin de \"Who is Not Without Sin\", Arthur ramène de Flatneck Station un [[orville-swanson|révérend Swanson]] ivre et le dépose sur son lit. Susan s'approche et demande ce qui s'est passé. Arthur répond que c'est toujours la même histoire. Elle plaint Swanson, remercie Arthur et promet de garder un œil sur le révérend. Le Red Dead Wiki la mentionne aussi dans \"A Strange Kindness\", la mission qui conduit au départ du gang vers le sud et Clemens Point, mais la page de la mission ne la nomme pas. Les scènes de camp de ce chapitre, dont la fête pour le retour de [[sean-macguire|Sean MacGuire]], sont traitées dans la rubrique Relations.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 3: Clemens Point", "Chapitre 3 : Clemens Point"), "chapter": 3},
    {"p": two("At Clemens Point, on the shore of Flat Iron Lake, the camp scenes with Dutch and Molly are covered under Relationships. At the end of \"Blessed are the Peacemakers\", Arthur escapes from the O'Driscolls who held him captive and rides back to camp badly wounded. Dutch calls for Miss Grimshaw and Swanson. Susan says to get him to bed, and Dutch asks her to sit with him for a while. She agrees and tells Arthur that he will be fine now that he is home. The Red Dead Wiki lists her in \"Blood Feuds, Ancient and Modern\", the attack on Braithwaite Manor, but the mission page does not name her.",
              "À Clemens Point, au bord du lac Flat Iron, les scènes de camp avec Dutch et Molly sont traitées dans la rubrique Relations. À la fin de \"Blessed are the Peacemakers\", Arthur échappe aux O'Driscoll qui le retenaient prisonnier et rentre au camp grièvement blessé. Dutch appelle Miss Grimshaw et Swanson à l'aide. Susan dit de le mettre au lit, et Dutch lui demande de rester un moment auprès de lui. Elle accepte et rassure Arthur : maintenant qu'il est rentré, il va s'en sortir. Le Red Dead Wiki la mentionne dans \"Blood Feuds, Ancient and Modern\", l'attaque du manoir Braithwaite, mais la page de la mission ne la nomme pas.")},
    {"p": two("\"The Battle of Shady Belle\" opens at Clemens Point, where the Pinkerton agents [[andrew-milton|Andrew Milton]] and [[edgar-ross|Edgar Ross]] walk into camp. Milton offers the others three days to disappear if Dutch surrenders to him. Dutch raises his hands in mock acceptance while the gang loads its guns, and Susan tells Dutch that it is time for his new friend to leave. Milton warns them that he will return with fifty men, and the gang moves to Shady Belle, an abandoned plantation house near Saint Denis. When the caravan arrives, after Arthur and [[john-marston|John Marston]] have cleared the house of Lemoyne Raiders and dumped the bodies in the swamp, Dutch asks Miss Grimshaw and Pearson to work their magic on the new camp.",
              "\"The Battle of Shady Belle\" commence à Clemens Point, où les agents de la Pinkerton [[andrew-milton|Andrew Milton]] et [[edgar-ross|Edgar Ross]] entrent dans le camp. Milton propose de laisser aux autres trois jours pour disparaître si Dutch se rend. Dutch lève les mains en feignant d'accepter pendant que le gang charge ses armes, et Susan lui fait savoir qu'il est temps que son nouvel ami s'en aille. Milton promet de revenir avec cinquante hommes, et le gang déménage à Shady Belle, une plantation abandonnée près de Saint-Denis. À l'arrivée du convoi, une fois qu'Arthur et [[john-marston|John Marston]] ont chassé de la maison les Lemoyne Raiders et jeté leurs cadavres dans le marais, Dutch demande à Miss Grimshaw et à Pearson d'opérer leur magie sur le nouveau camp.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 4: Saint Denis", "Chapitre 4 : Saint-Denis"), "chapter": 4},
    {"p": two("In \"No, No and Thrice, No\", Arthur is smoking and talking with Mary-Beth when Susan interrupts them. Tilly has been taken by the Foreman Brothers, the gang she once rode with, and Susan knows where: Radley's House, in Scarlett Meadows. She takes a revolver and rides there with Arthur in a wagon. What she says on the way depends on the order of play: before [[jack-marston|Jack Marston]] is brought back, she remarks that first Jack and now Tilly have been kidnapped; after it, she notes that [[kieran-duffy|Kieran Duffy]] has not been seen for some time. At the house, Susan engages the only guard outside in conversation, then stabs him. Arthur goes in, surprises two more Foremans and finds Tilly bound to a chair upstairs, and sets her free.",
              "Dans \"No, No and Thrice, No\", Arthur fume une cigarette en discutant avec Mary-Beth quand Susan les interrompt. Tilly a été enlevée par les Foreman Brothers, la bande avec laquelle elle chevauchait autrefois, et Susan sait où la trouver : à Radley's House, dans les Scarlett Meadows. Elle prend un revolver et s'y rend avec Arthur en chariot. Ce qu'elle dit en route dépend de l'ordre des missions : si Jack n'a pas encore été retrouvé, elle relève qu'après [[jack-marston|Jack Marston]], c'est au tour de Tilly d'être enlevée ; s'il l'a été, elle remarque qu'on n'a pas vu [[kieran-duffy|Kieran Duffy]] depuis un moment. Sur place, Susan fait la conversation au seul garde posté dehors, puis le poignarde. Arthur entre, prend deux autres Foreman par surprise et trouve Tilly ligotée sur une chaise à l'étage, qu'il détache.")},
    {"p": two("Tilly tells them that Anthony Foreman and his men took her and that some of them have gone out hunting. Anthony and two riders are seen fleeing from the back of the house, and Tilly asks for Anthony to be brought back alive. Arthur and Susan give chase on horseback and kill the two riders; according to the mission page's tips, if Arthur is too slow, Susan shoots one of them herself. Arthur ropes Anthony and brings him back hogtied; Susan leads his horse back. Tilly and Susan confront him and order him to leave Tilly alone, which he promises once Arthur threatens him. According to the Red Dead Wiki's character page, Susan urges Arthur to slit his throat. The mission page says she tells Arthur the decision is his before taking Tilly back to camp. The player chooses whether Arthur kills or spares him.",
              "Tilly leur raconte qu'Anthony Foreman et ses hommes l'ont enlevée, et que certains sont partis chasser. On voit Anthony et deux cavaliers s'enfuir par l'arrière de la maison, et Tilly demande qu'on lui ramène Anthony vivant. Arthur et Susan se lancent à leur poursuite à cheval et abattent les deux cavaliers ; d'après les conseils de la page de la mission, si Arthur tarde trop, Susan en abat un elle-même. Arthur attrape Anthony au lasso et le ramène ligoté ; Susan ramène sa monture. Tilly et Susan l'affrontent et lui ordonnent de laisser Tilly tranquille, ce qu'il promet quand Arthur le menace. Selon la page du personnage sur le Red Dead Wiki, Susan pousse Arthur à lui trancher la gorge. La page de la mission indique au contraire qu'elle laisse la décision à Arthur avant de ramener Tilly au camp. C'est le joueur qui choisit si Arthur le tue ou l'épargne.")},
    {"p": two("In \"Horsemen, Apocalypses\", the O'Driscolls attack Shady Belle in force. According to the character page, she fires on the attackers with a double-barreled shotgun until Dutch sends her into the house. The mission page says the camp's non-fighting members rush into the house, and an image on that page shows her taking cover there with Mary-Beth, [[leopold-strauss|Leopold Strauss]], [[abigail-marston|Abigail Roberts]] and Jack. Afterwards, the same page says, Dutch puts her and Pearson in charge of clearing the O'Driscoll corpses from the grounds.",
              "Dans \"Horsemen, Apocalypses\", les O'Driscoll attaquent Shady Belle en nombre. D'après la page du personnage, elle fait feu sur les assaillants au fusil à deux coups jusqu'à ce que Dutch l'envoie dans la maison. La page de la mission précise que les membres du camp qui ne combattent pas se précipitent à l'intérieur, et une image de cette page la montre à l'abri dans la maison avec Mary-Beth, [[leopold-strauss|Leopold Strauss]], [[abigail-marston|Abigail Roberts]] et Jack. L'assaut repoussé, Dutch charge Susan et Pearson de débarrasser le domaine des cadavres des O'Driscoll, toujours selon la page du personnage.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 5: Guarma", "Chapitre 5 : Guarma"), "chapter": 5},
    {"p": two("Susan stays behind while Dutch, Arthur and the others are stranded on Guarma after the Saint Denis bank robbery. In \"Fleeting Joy\", Arthur rejoins the gang at Lakay, in the bayou, and the Pinkertons attack the camp; the mission page does not name her. Once the fight is over, she tells the gang to pack up before the Pinkertons come back, according to the wiki's list of camp events. \"That's Murfree Country\", the last mission of the chapter, takes the gang to Beaver Hollow, a cave in Roanoke Ridge that Arthur and [[charles-smith|Charles Smith]] clear of the Murfree Brood.",
              "Susan reste en arrière pendant que Dutch, Arthur et les autres sont coincés à Guarma après le braquage de la banque de Saint-Denis. Dans \"Fleeting Joy\", Arthur retrouve le gang à Lakay, dans le bayou, et la Pinkerton attaque le camp ; la page de la mission ne la nomme pas. Une fois le combat terminé, elle ordonne à tout le monde de plier bagage avant le retour de la Pinkerton, d'après la liste des scènes de camp du wiki. \"That's Murfree Country\", la dernière mission du chapitre, conduit le gang à Beaver Hollow, une grotte de Roanoke Ridge qu'Arthur et [[charles-smith|Charles Smith]] débarrassent des Murfree.")},
    {"p": two("While the new camp is being set up, Uncle arrives with Molly O'Shea, who is drunk. In front of the gang, Molly claims that she told the Pinkertons about the Saint Denis bank job, and she taunts Dutch. Dutch goes to kill her, and Arthur asks him to let her go. Susan fires a shotgun into Molly's stomach, killing her. She tells Arthur that Molly knew the rules, and tells Bill and Pearson to burn the corpse. The killing ends the chapter. The camp's reactions, among them Karen calling Susan a murderer, are covered under Relationships.",
              "Pendant l'installation du nouveau camp, Uncle arrive avec Molly O'Shea, ivre. Devant le gang, Molly affirme avoir renseigné la Pinkerton sur le braquage de la banque de Saint-Denis, et elle nargue Dutch. Dutch s'apprête à la tuer, et Arthur lui demande de la laisser partir. Susan tire sur Molly au fusil de chasse, en plein ventre, et la tue. Elle rappelle à Arthur que Molly connaissait les règles, puis ordonne à Bill et à Pearson de brûler le corps. Ce meurtre clôt le chapitre. Les réactions du camp, dont Karen qui traite Susan de meurtrière, sont traitées dans la rubrique Relations.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 6: Beaver Hollow", "Chapitre 6 : Beaver Hollow"), "chapter": 6},
    {"p": two("Susan's exchanges with Dutch, Tilly and Jack in the Beaver Hollow camp are covered under Relationships. In \"Red Dead Redemption\", the last mission of the chapter, Arthur learns from Milton, before Abigail shoots the agent, that the Pinkertons questioned Molly a couple of times and that she never said a word, whereas they picked up Micah when the gang came back from Guarma and he has worked for them ever since. When Arthur rides back into camp, Micah is hurrying Susan and the others to pack, and she answers that they are doing their best. Arthur says that Micah is the rat. Micah calls it a lie, and the two men draw on each other. John, back from prison, accuses Dutch of leaving him to die, and Arthur tells everyone to pick a side.",
              "Les échanges de Susan avec Dutch, Tilly et Jack au camp de Beaver Hollow sont traités dans la rubrique Relations. Dans \"Red Dead Redemption\", dernière mission du chapitre, Arthur apprend de Milton, avant qu'Abigail n'abatte l'agent, que la Pinkerton a cuisiné Molly plus d'une fois sans lui arracher un mot, alors que Micah, arrêté au retour du gang de Guarma, travaille pour elle depuis. Quand Arthur revient au camp, Micah presse Susan et les autres de remballer, et elle répond qu'ils font de leur mieux. Arthur affirme que Micah est le mouchard. Micah dément, et les deux hommes se mettent en joue. John, sorti de prison, reproche à Dutch de l'avoir laissé mourir, et Arthur somme chacun de choisir son camp.")},
    {"p": two("When Micah tells Arthur to be quiet, Susan levels her shotgun at Micah and orders him to be quiet himself and put his gun down. According to the Red Dead Wiki, she is the only one besides John to side openly with Arthur. [[javier-escuella|Javier Escuella]] calls out that Pinkertons are coming fast. Susan turns at the warning, and Micah shoots her dead. In the transcript, Dutch says nothing about her: he demands to know who is with him and who is betraying him, and the Pinkertons open fire. If Arthur goes back for the money with low honor, he begs Dutch, after Dutch arrives and stops Micah from finishing him, to kill Micah: \"Not Molly... not Miss Grimshaw... not even Colm.\" This line belongs to that ending only. After the gang falls apart, Charles Smith returns to Beaver Hollow, collects Susan's body and Arthur's, and buries them.",
              "Quand Micah ordonne à Arthur de se taire, Susan braque son fusil sur Micah et lui ordonne de se taire lui-même et de baisser son arme. D'après le Red Dead Wiki, elle est la seule, avec John, à prendre ouvertement le parti d'Arthur. [[javier-escuella|Javier Escuella]] crie que des agents de la Pinkerton arrivent à toute vitesse. Susan se retourne à l'alerte, et Micah l'abat. Dans la transcription, Dutch n'a pas un mot pour elle : il exige de savoir qui est avec lui et qui le trahit, puis la Pinkerton ouvre le feu. Si Arthur, avec un honneur bas, retourne chercher l'argent, il supplie Dutch, arrivé à temps pour arrêter Micah, de tuer Micah : \"Not Molly... not Miss Grimshaw... not even Colm.\" (\"Ni Molly... ni Miss Grimshaw... ni même Colm.\") Cette réplique n'existe que dans cette fin. Après la dislocation du gang, Charles Smith revient à Beaver Hollow, récupère les corps de Susan et d'Arthur et les enterre.")},

    # ================================================================ Epilogue
    {"h3": two("Red Dead Redemption 2, epilogue (1907)", "Red Dead Redemption 2, épilogue (1907)"), "year": "1907"},
    {"h4": two("Epilogue 1: Pronghorn Ranch", "Épilogue 1 : Pronghorn Ranch"), "chapter": "E1"},
    {"p": two("In 1907, once \"Simple Pleasures\" is done, John can visit Susan's grave. It stands on a hilltop above the railroad line, southwest of Elysian Pool, in Roanoke Ridge (New Hanover). According to the character page, her necklace hangs on the wooden cross. Arthur dies soon after Susan, so John is the only character who can visit it. It is one of the graves needed for the Paying Respects trophy.",
              "En 1907, une fois \"Simple Pleasures\" terminée, John peut se recueillir sur la tombe de Susan. Elle se dresse en haut d'une colline, au-dessus de la voie ferrée, au sud-ouest d'Elysian Pool, à Roanoke Ridge (New Hanover). D'après la page du personnage, son collier est accroché à la croix de bois. Arthur mourant peu après Susan, John est le seul personnage à pouvoir s'y rendre. Elle fait partie des tombes à visiter pour le trophée Paying Respects.")},
]
